# GuvFX FX ingestion schedule (Bank of England XUDLUSS, GBP->USD).
#
# TIMEZONE: the production host and the backend container both run UTC (Etc/UTC). London is UTC in winter (GMT)
# and UTC+1 in summer (BST). The BoE publishes the daily XUDLUSS spot ~midday London (T+1). 15:00 UTC is safely
# AFTER that window in BOTH GMT (15:00 London) and BST (16:00 London), year-round, so one daily run reliably
# captures the previous London business day's published rate. Weekends/holidays have no new publication, so a
# run then simply finds nothing new (idempotent duplicate-skip) - harmless.
#
# Only Bank of England is scheduled. FRED (Fed H.10 DEXUSUK) is deliberately NOT scheduled: it currently times
# out from the production container and BoE is the governed primary (PORTFOLIO_FX_SOURCE_PRIORITY=BOE,FED_H10).
#
# run_fx_boe_ingest.sh: single-instance (flock), bounded timeout, bounded retries+backoff, append-only, idempotent.
# run_fx_freshness_check.sh: read-only health monitor; quiet when HEALTHY and fresh, FX_FRESHNESS_ALERT + non-zero
# when STALE/EMPTY or aging past the warn threshold (before the 7-day refusal boundary).
#
# Managed by deploy/fx-ingestion/install_fx_ingestion_cron.sh (end-anchored markers below).

# Daily BoE ingestion at 15:00 UTC (after the London publication window).
0 15 * * * /home/ubuntu/guvfx-app/deploy/fx-ingestion/run_fx_boe_ingest.sh >> /var/log/guvfx/fetch_fx_boe.log 2>&1 # guvfx-fetch-fx-boe

# Freshness monitor: after the ingest (16:00 UTC) and a morning check (08:00 UTC).
0 16 * * * /home/ubuntu/guvfx-app/deploy/fx-ingestion/run_fx_freshness_check.sh >> /var/log/guvfx/fx_freshness.log 2>&1 # guvfx-fx-freshness-pm
0 8  * * * /home/ubuntu/guvfx-app/deploy/fx-ingestion/run_fx_freshness_check.sh >> /var/log/guvfx/fx_freshness.log 2>&1 # guvfx-fx-freshness-am
